        description: `Home to the last two northern white rhinos on Earth and Kenya's highest concentration of predators — Ol Pejeta Conservancy is conservation at its most powerful. Expect Big Five encounters across open savannah backed by the snow-capped peaks of Mt. Kenya, a visit to the chimpanzee sanctuary, and up-close moments with critically endangered black rhinos in the dedicated rhino enclosure. Lions, leopards, hyenas, and the rare African wild dog roam freely here. This is a safari with purpose — where every game drive supports one of Africa's most important conservation stories.`,
