                day: 4,
                title: 'Mnemba Atoll Snorkelling & Dolphin Tour',
                description: `7:30 AM — After an early breakfast, you board a boat for the trip to Mnemba Atoll — a small coral island surrounded by some of the finest snorkelling waters in East Africa. The boat ride takes roughly thirty minutes, and as you approach the atoll, the water shifts from deep oceanic blue to luminous turquoise over the coral reef below. Keep your eyes on the surface — pods of bottlenose dolphins frequently appear in these warm currents, their dorsal fins slicing through the glassy water before they leap in silver arcs.

Slipping into the warm water with mask and fins, you're surrounded by a kaleidoscope of tropical marine life — parrotfish in electric blues and greens, butterflyfish dancing through the coral branches, angelfish gliding with effortless grace, and trumpetfish hovering vertically among the sea fans. Green sea turtles rise from the seagrass beds to breathe, hovering at the surface for a moment before descending in a graceful spiral. The coral formations themselves are extraordinary — brain corals, branching staghorns, and table corals creating an underwater cityscape alive with movement and colour.

You'll snorkel two or three different reef sites through the morning, each with its own character. Between sites, the boat drifts and fresh tropical fruit is shared. By early afternoon you're back at your resort with the rest of the day at leisure — perhaps a beachside massage, a cold drink in the shade, or simply floating in the warm Indian Ocean reliving the underwater colours.`,
                meals: ['Breakfast', 'Dinner']
