                description: '## 45-min flight\n\n8:00 AM. Check in at Wilson Airport, Nairobi, for the scenic 45-minute flight south to Amboseli. As the light aircraft crosses the Athi Plains and the Kilimanjaro foothills, the mountain itself rises spectacularly ahead — its snow-capped peak piercing the morning sky. You land at the Amboseli airstrip where your guide greets you, and even from the tarmac the first elephant herds are visible moving across the plains. A short drive brings you to your safari lodge where you settle in and enjoy lunch. The afternoon game drive takes you straight into the action. Huge herds of elephants — Amboseli hosts over 1,500 — cross the dusty savannah with Kilimanjaro as an ever-present backdrop. Your guide navigates toward the swamps where hippos wallow, pelicans fish in the shallows, and Egyptian geese crowd the banks. The golden evening light makes every sighting feel cinematic. Return to your lodge for dinner beneath a sky full of stars.',
