                day: 2,
                title: 'Serengeti Plains',
                description: '6:00 AM. A full day in the Serengeti with no travel commitments — just uninterrupted wildlife viewing. The dawn drive heads to the open plains where cheetahs perch on termite mounds, scanning for prey in the cool morning air. Your guide navigates toward the kopjes — ancient granite outcrops that rise from the flat savannah like rocky islands. Lions use these as lookout posts, and the rocks themselves are alive with colourful agama lizards and small rock hyraxes. The Serengeti is the big cat capital of the world, and today is your chance for close encounters — perhaps a leopard returning to a kill cached in a tree, or a cheetah mother teaching her cubs to hunt. Enjoy a bush lunch in the shade, then spend the afternoon in a different sector of the park. During the Great Migration season, the moving herds of wildebeest are an overwhelming sight — millions of animals in a single, restless column stretching to the horizon. Return to camp under a sky thick with stars.',
