                description: `## ~35km | Approx. 45 mins

7:00 AM — Your C.A.T.S guide collects your group from Diani Beach hotels in a shared 4×4 Land Cruiser. The drive is short but dramatic — within 30 minutes the white-sand coastline gives way to the emerald-green ridges of Shimba Hills rising from the coastal plain. Enter through the main gate by 7:45 AM and immediately feel the temperature drop as the canopy closes overhead.

8:00 AM — Begin your game drive through Kenya's only coastal rainforest reserve. The morning light filters through giant fig trees and mvule hardwoods. Your guide scans the forest edges for the star attraction — the endangered sable antelope, a magnificent beast with swept-back scimitar horns found nowhere else in Kenya. Shimba Hills is their last stronghold.

9:30 AM — Stop at the Sheldrick Falls viewpoint and descend on a guided 45-minute forest hike. The trail winds through buttress-rooted trees draped in moss and orchids, alive with birdsong — watch for the green-headed oriole and Fischer's turaco flashing crimson wings overhead. The falls cascade 21 metres into a clear pool surrounded by ferns — a hidden world minutes from the beach.

11:00 AM — Continue your game drive through the open grasslands on the reserve's western plateau. African elephants are regular here, often seen in family groups crossing clearings. Leopard, buffalo, waterbuck, and bushbuck inhabit the forest margins. Giraffe browse acacia woodlands along the ridgeline, silhouetted against panoramic views of the Indian Ocean below.

12:30 PM — Enjoy a packed lunch at a scenic picnic site overlooking the reserve, with the Kenyan coast shimmering on the horizon.

1:30 PM — Afternoon game loop through the southern sector. Angola colobus monkeys swing through the canopy, their black-and-white mantles catching the dappled light. Sykes' monkeys chatter in the undergrowth. If luck favours, your guide may spot a leopard resting in the fork of a strangler fig.

3:30 PM — Exit the reserve and begin the short drive back to Diani Beach. Arrive at your hotel by 4:15 PM — refreshed, inspired, and back in time for a sunset swim.`,
