                description: `## ~100km | Approx. 2 hrs (transfer) + game drives

6:00 AM — Dawn game drive in Tsavo East before departing westward. Cross the Nairobi-Mombasa highway into Tsavo West — and the landscape transforms. Green volcanic hills replace the flat red plains. The Chyulu Hills create a dramatic backdrop.

9:30 AM — Arrive at Mzima Springs — one of Kenya's most extraordinary natural phenomena. 250 million litres of crystal-clear water bubble up daily from volcanic rock, creating pools teeming with hippos and Nile crocodiles. An underwater observation chamber lets you watch hippos glide past in impossibly clear water — a surreal experience.

11:00 AM — Drive to the Shetani Lava Flow — a jet-black river of volcanic rock frozen mid-flow across the landscape. Walk across the 200-year-old lava field (Shetani means "devil" in Swahili — locals believed only the devil could produce such destruction). The Shetani Caves nearby are worth exploring.

12:30 PM — Lunch with views of the Chyulu Hills. The afternoon game drive explores Tsavo West's predator-rich western plains. Lions and cheetah hunt the open grasslands, while leopards favour the rocky outcrops. Elephant herds cross between watering points, and giraffe browse the acacia woodland.

3:30 PM — Exit the park and begin the drive back to the coast. Arrive in Diani Beach by 6:30 PM.`,
