  title: '3-Day Aberdares Rainforest Safari',
  description: `Venture into the emerald heart of Kenya's highlands on this enchanting 3-day Aberdares rainforest safari. Aberdare National Park protects a vast swathe of ancient montane forest, bamboo groves, and moorland plateaux rising above 3,000 metres. Waterfalls cascade through moss-draped ravines, and the forest floor is carpeted with ferns and orchids — a world apart from the sun-baked savannahs that define most Kenya safaris.

The Aberdares are home to a unique cast of wildlife adapted to the cool, misty highlands. Giant forest hogs — the world's largest wild pigs — emerge at dusk to root around floodlit waterholes. Black rhinos browse in bamboo thickets. Leopards, rarely seen elsewhere by day, prowl the forest tracks. And the elusive eastern bongo, one of Africa's most endangered antelopes, haunts the deepest groves.

A highlight of this safari is a night at a legendary tree lodge, where you watch wildlife from elevated viewing decks as elephants, buffalo, and hyenas visit the floodlit waterhole and salt lick below. This is a safari for those who crave atmosphere, altitude, and the thrill of the unexpected.`,
