  title: '4-Day Meru National Park Safari',
  description: `Journey to one of Kenya's most beautiful and least-visited national parks on this immersive 4-day Meru National Park safari. Immortalised by Joy Adamson's Born Free story of Elsa the lioness, Meru remains a raw and authentic wilderness where towering doum palms line the Tana River, emerald swamps attract hippo pods, and vast grasslands stretch to the blue Nyambeni Hills on the horizon.

Meru National Park offers a safari experience far removed from the crowds of more famous reserves. Here, you may be the only vehicle at a leopard sighting or have an entire riverbank of elephants to yourself. The park's Rhino Sanctuary, managed in partnership with the Kenya Wildlife Service, protects both black and white rhinos behind a secure perimeter, offering outstanding close-range viewing of these magnificent creatures.

The diversity of habitats — from riverine forest and swamp to open savannah and rocky kopjes — supports a remarkable variety of wildlife. Lesser kudu, reticulated giraffe, Grevy's zebra, and gerenuk share the landscape with lions, cheetahs, and wild dogs. This is a safari for those who value wilderness, solitude, and the thrill of true exploration.`,
